# MASTER PROMPT — YOUTUBE MARKETPLACE FRONTEND

## 1. Project Objective

Build a complete, production-quality, responsive YouTube Marketplace website with a professional design and fully functional frontend.

The platform will offer YouTube-related creator services, compliant audience-growth promotion packages, YouTube channel marketplace listings, and YouTube video marketplace listings.

This is not a static UI demo. Every button, form, filter, cart action, navigation link, and admin control must work correctly and connect to the backend API.

## 2. Mandatory Development Workflow

Follow this workflow strictly:

1. ANALYZE the existing project before changing anything.
2. Identify the framework, dependencies, routes, components, styling conventions, environment variables, and existing functionality.
3. Create a detailed implementation plan and a checklist/TODO roadmap.
4. Identify API requirements and coordinate with the backend contract defined in the separate backend prompt.
5. Implement one phase at a time.
6. Test each completed phase before proceeding.
7. Update the TODO checklist as tasks are completed.
8. At the end of each phase, report completed tasks, tests, remaining issues, and the next phase.
9. Do not claim a feature is complete unless it has been implemented and verified.
10. Do not unnecessarily rewrite existing files or replace working functionality.

Do not begin implementation until the analysis and plan are complete. After producing the plan, proceed with implementation without waiting for approval unless a genuine blocker exists.

## 3. Technology Stack

- Next.js App Router
- React
- TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS
- shadcn/ui where appropriate
- lucide-react icons
- react-hook-form and Zod where useful
- A suitable notification library, reusing existing dependencies if available
- Backend integration through a centralized typed API client
- MongoDB is accessed ONLY through the backend API, never directly from the browser

Reuse installed dependencies and existing conventions wherever possible. Avoid unnecessary libraries.

## 4. Design Requirements

Create a premium, modern, professional YouTube Marketplace UI.

Visual direction:
- Primary background: dark navy, approximately #050B14
- Secondary background: #0B1220
- Accent red: #FF1744
- White service cards and clean light content sections
- Neutral gray text and borders
- Consistent typography, spacing, border radii, shadows, and hover states
- Lucide icons instead of random emoji icons
- High-quality thumbnails and properly optimized images
- Subtle transitions and animations without harming performance

The design should be inspired by the provided reference image but must be original, polished, and consistent across all pages.

Do not make the entire website dark. Use a balanced combination of dark hero/header areas and clean, light service/package sections.

